    rdfs:label "miconazole" ;
    definition: "A racemate composed of equimolar amounts of (<i>R</i>)- and (<i>S</i>)-miconazole. Used (as its nitrate salt) to treat skin infections such as athlete's foot, jock itch, ringworm and other fungal skin infections. It inhibits the synthesis of ergosterol, a critical component of fungal cell membranes." ;
