    rdfs:label "dinitrogen oxide" ;
    definition: "A nitrogen oxide consisting of linear unsymmetrical molecules with formula N<small><sub>2</sub></small>O. While it is the most used gaseous anaesthetic in the world, its major commercial use, due to its solubility under pressure in vegetable fats combined with its non-toxicity in low concentrations, is as an aerosol spray propellant and aerating agent for canisters of 'whipped' cream." ;
