    rdfs:label "methoxsalen" ;
    definition: "A member of the class of psoralens that is 7<em>H</em>-furo[3,2-<em>g</em>]chromen-7-one in which the 9 position is substituted by a methoxy group. It is a constituent of the fruits of <em>Ammi majus</em>. Like other psoralens, trioxsalen causes photosensitization of the skin. It is administered topically or orally in conjunction with UV-A for phototherapy treatment of vitiligo and severe psoriasis." ;
